  "body": "BODY:\n\n## Summary\n\n\n\n`@memtensor/memos-local-plugin@2.0.20` (DSH adapter) still writes messages with the legacy V3 source shape `source.kind: \"plugin\"`. dsh 0.2.1-rc.2 session format **V4** rejects any runtime-written message whose `source.kind === \"plugin\"`:\n\n\n\n```\n\nSessionFormatError: format v4 message requires a producer-owned source kind\n\n  (@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-format-v3-to-v4/lib/index.js:126)\n\n```\n\n\n\nResult: **every conversation turn fails with UNKNOWN error** as soon as the plugin injects its recall message — the harness is completely unusable with this plugin installed.\n\n\n\n## Offending code (v2.0.20, dist/adapters/deepseek-harness/)\n\n\n\n1. `index.js` (~line 301) — per-turn recall message:\n\n```js\n\ncreateRecallMessage: (text) => createUserMessage({\n\n    content: [{ type: \"text\", text }],\n\n    source: {\n\n        kind: \"plugin\",              // ← rejected by V4 validator\n\n        plugin: DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_PLUGIN,\n\n        form: \"recall\",\n\n    },\n\n}),\n\n```\n\n2. `host-llm.js` (~line 220) — host LLM messages:\n\n```js\n\nsource: { kind: \"plugin\", plugin: HOST_LLM_MESSAGE_SOURCE },  // ← rejected\n\n```\n\n\n\nThe V3→V4 migration rewrites historical sessions, but **runtime writes are hard-rejected**.\n\n\n\n## Expected fix\n\n\n\nUse the producer-owned form that dsh itself maps unknown plugins to:\n\n\n\n```js\n\nkind: \"plugin:memos-local-memory\"   // instead of kind: \"plugin\", plugin: \"...\"\n\n```\n\n\n\nWe verified locally: replacing both sites with `kind: \"plugin:memos-local-memory\"` makes all turns pass again (syntax-checked, zero residual `kind: \"plugin\"` in dist, web profile back to normal).\n\n\n\n## Secondary issue: peer range pins plugin to dsh <0.2.0\n\n\n\nThe plugin's peer requirements (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent` etc. `>=0.1.0-rc.5 <0.2.0`) make dsh 0.2.1-rc.2 **skip the bundle at startup** (\"incompatible ... Exact-version exemption: not active\"). Users must hand-grant `dsh plugin allow-version`. Please widen the range (or republish) once the V4 kind fix is in, otherwise the plugin silently doesn't load on current dsh.\n\n\n\n## Environment\n\n\n\n- dsh 0.2.1-rc.2, plugin @memtensor/memos-local-plugin@2.0.20 (latest on npm as of 2026-10-23)\n\n- Reproduced on 3 machines (Linux x86_64, macOS arm64, Linux aarch64) — deterministic, 100% repro on any new turn\n\n- Session data on affected hosts was not corrupted (rejection happens before persistence)",
